# OpenSpec starts at explore

Do not use Cursor Plan mode or `/plan` for spec-driven work. Start with `/opsx-explore`, then `/opsx-propose <id>` → `/opsx-apply <id>` → `/opsx-archive` only when asked. Do not edit product code for that feature until an OpenSpec change exists under `openspec/changes/<id>/`.

```
# ❌ BAD
/plan I want a new feature to update the customer email in the invoice detail customer card.

# ✅ GOOD
/opsx-explore I want a new feature to update the customer email in the invoice detail customer card. Don’t implement email validation.
/opsx-propose invoice-detail-email
/opsx-apply invoice-detail-email
```

Cursor Desktop spelling is hyphenated (`/opsx-explore`). Validate with `npx openspec validate --changes --strict` before apply. Do not archive unless asked.

OpenSpec is local in the 101 track. Linear is a 201 beat; do not pull Linear MCP or Cloud Agents into a 101 change.
